-attachment uses a replicated `Game1WeaponGrip` Attachment generated during Studio sync. Its point is taken from the imported model pivot and its frame is canonicalized to world XYZ. every weapon uses the same Studio/runtime equip basis: the target weapon socket is rotated -90 degrees around its local X axis before grip alignment. this is a global weapon-system rule, not per-asset metadata. melee uses the right weapon socket and bow uses the left weapon socket. on each runtime clone the server strips any stale per-weapon grip rotation left by older revisions, then alignment uses the full current grip frame with `desiredSocket * currentGrip^-1`. this produces an absolute rigid delta rather than accumulating rotation every render frame. the client follows the animated socket with the same stable calculation.
+attachment is runtime-canonical. on every equip the server discards any stale `Game1WeaponGrip` orientation from the Studio template (or creates the grip if an old template has none), preserves only its authored grip point, and rebuilds one `Game1WeaponGrip` with canonical world XYZ axes. every weapon therefore uses one solver and never falls back to `Model:PivotTo(socketFrame)`. the target weapon socket is rotated -90 degrees around its local X axis before `desiredSocket * currentGrip^-1` alignment. melee uses the right weapon socket and bow uses the left weapon socket. this global rule is independent of per-asset pivot orientation and cannot accumulate rotation per frame.
